# Generate the modulated structure according to the X3- mode (mode 1):
# X3-(0;a), Cmcm
crystod-phonon --modulation --yaml phonopy_params.yaml --qpoint 0 0 0.5 --mode 1 --amplitude 0.3
# -> MPOSCAR_X_mode1_X3-_Cmcm


# The star of X has two arms, (0,0,1/2) and (1/2,1/2,0) (the star printed
# above). Mode 1 frozen into both arms with equal amplitudes is X3-(a;a),
# P4_2/mnm; unequal amplitudes give X3-(a;b), Pnnm -- the rows of
# crystod-group --parent I4/mmm --irrep X3-. An arm may be written as any
# equivalent q: --qpoint2 -0.5 0.5 0 (the same point shifted by a reciprocal
# lattice vector) writes the same structure.
crystod-phonon --modulation --yaml phonopy_params.yaml --qpoint1 0 0 0.5 --mode1 1 --amplitude1 0.3 --qpoint2 0.5 0.5 0 --mode2 1 --amplitude2 0.3

