# Every order-parameter direction of the two lowest X levels (X3-, X4-) at
# once, each written with the --modulation command that reproduces it:
# MPOSCAR_X_X3-_0_a_Cmcm, MPOSCAR_X_X3-_a_a_P4_2mnm, MPOSCAR_X_X3-_a_b_Pnnm,
# MPOSCAR_X_X4-_0_a_Cmme, MPOSCAR_X_X4-_a_a_P4_2mcm, MPOSCAR_X_X4-_a_b_Pccm.
# The levels are stable, so --threshold raises the cut above them.
crystod-phonon --subgroup -c 139_PPOSCAR_Sr3Ti2O7 --dim "4 4 4" --qpoint X --threshold 3.0 --modulate

# --modulation reports the space group at 0.1 A by default; add
# --tolerance 1e-5 to check it strictly. The two (a;b) structures, whose
# second arm has the amplitude 0.16434, read as their (a;a) groups at 0.1
# (P4_2/mnm and P4_2/mcm) and as Pnnm and Pccm at 1e-5.

